<metadata><name>Elk Lake and Gold Butte Lookout from Dunlap Saddle</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:231-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.819492" lon="-122.089386"><ele>1144.7</ele><name>Dunlap Saddle</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:dunlap-saddle (OSM node 40372201, fork of 4697 and NF 451); confidence: high; pdf_page: 234; book_elev_ft: 3748; quote: then 1.7 miles to Dunlap Saddle at 3,748 feet. This is the end of driving</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.825193" lon="-122.124965"><ele>1169.6</ele><name>Elk Lake, north shore (Road 4697 at the Battle Ax Creek Trailhead)</name><desc>source: OSM: end of way 552501044 Forest Road 4697 at Battle Ax Creek Trailhead (node 14158679917), north shore of Elk Lake (way 188553302), Elk Lake Campground 400 m SW; 2.0 mi by road from the saddle as map 47's '2.0'; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 234; book_elev_ft: 3720; quote: Ski west over easy terrain 2 miles to the lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.819492" lon="-122.089386"><ele>1144.7</ele><name>Dunlap Saddle (back)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 234; book_elev_ft: 3748; quote: from Dunlap Saddle</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.805207" lon="-122.083645"><ele>1407.4</ele><name>Gold Butte Lookout</name><desc>source: OSM way 496817151 Gold Butte Lookout (GNIS peak node 357309720 beside it); confidence: high; pdf_page: 234; book_elev_ft: 4618; quote: follow a steep, primitive road southeast 1.3 miles, then a steep trail to the Gold Butte summit fire-lookout cabin at 4,618 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.819492" lon="-122.089386"><ele>1144.7</ele><name>Dunlap Saddle (end)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 234; book_elev_ft: 3748; quote: a climb of 900 feet from the saddle</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Elk Lake and Gold Butte Lookout from Dunlap Saddle</name><desc>1. Dunlap Saddle -&gt; Elk Lake, north shore (Road 4697 at the Battle Ax Creek Trailhead): osm (high), 2.04 mi | 2. Elk Lake, north shore (Road 4697 at the Battle Ax Creek Trailhead) -&gt; Dunlap Saddle (back): osm (high), 2.04 mi | 3. Dunlap Saddle (back) -&gt; Gold Butte Lookout: osm (medium), 1.57 mi | 4. Gold Butte Lookout -&gt; Dunlap Saddle (end): osm (medium), 1.57 mi</desc>
